# zsh-abbr user abbreviations — seeded from zsh/aliases.zsh.
#
# Loaded via $ABBR_USER_ABBREVIATIONS_FILE (set in zsh/zinit.zsh). Unlike an
# alias, an abbreviation expands inline as you type (SPACE/ENTER), so the full
# command is what runs AND what lands in history. Manage with `abbr add NAME=…`,
# `abbr erase NAME`, `abbr list`.
#
# NOTE: abbr rewrites this file on `abbr add`/`erase` and does not preserve
# comments — this header and the section breaks below survive only until the
# first such mutation.

